00:36:27.000 --> 00:36:31.000
Since you were, I don't know, one year old, you always heard it.

00:36:31.000 --> 00:36:33.000
You know it.

00:36:33.000 --> 00:36:35.000
Association of things.

00:36:35.000 --> 00:36:37.000
Natural.

00:36:37.000 --> 00:36:39.000
Remember this, Yom Echad.

00:36:39.000 --> 00:36:41.000
It's unique.

00:36:41.000 --> 00:36:43.000
Without precedent, without this.

00:36:45.000 --> 00:36:47.000
You cannot measure it.

00:36:47.000 --> 00:36:49.000
You have no means to measure it against something.

00:36:51.000 --> 00:36:53.000
God is Echad.

00:36:53.000 --> 00:36:58.000
The thought occurred to me that Echad also is not singular in terms.

00:36:58.000 --> 00:36:59.000
Exactly.

00:36:59.000 --> 00:37:02.000
It doesn't mean mathematically singular.

00:37:02.000 --> 00:37:05.000
That's not the object of the Echad.

00:37:05.000 --> 00:37:10.000
It's singular in the sense of being unique.

00:37:10.000 --> 00:37:15.000
The uniqueness more than the number, than the arithmetic of it.

00:37:15.000 --> 00:37:20.000
Could you carry that to the premise that within this uniqueness,

00:37:20.000 --> 00:37:23.000
everything is there for that which is to come?

00:37:23.000 --> 00:37:24.000
Maybe.

00:37:24.000 --> 00:37:25.000
Who knows?

00:37:25.000 --> 00:37:27.000
This already transcends.

00:37:27.000 --> 00:37:29.000
This goes into mysticism and so on.

00:37:30.000 --> 00:37:32.000
I don't know.

00:37:34.000 --> 00:37:39.000
But I just wanted you to see the richness of the language

00:37:39.000 --> 00:37:42.000
because it allows so many associations.

00:37:44.000 --> 00:37:46.000
Let's go back.

00:37:49.000 --> 00:37:51.000
By the time it ends, you'll be dizzy.

00:37:51.000 --> 00:37:53.000
You'll have to walk in the streets.

00:37:54.000 --> 00:37:55.000
Let's go back.

00:37:55.000 --> 00:37:56.000
What does it say?

00:37:56.000 --> 00:37:58.000
And there was evening.

00:37:58.000 --> 00:38:00.000
And there was morning.

00:38:01.000 --> 00:38:02.000
Yom Echad.

00:38:04.000 --> 00:38:08.000
Now, in biblical tradition,

00:38:09.000 --> 00:38:11.000
when does the day begin?

00:38:16.000 --> 00:38:18.000
And when does it finish?

00:38:19.000 --> 00:38:20.000
Sanna.

00:38:20.000 --> 00:38:22.000
From Sanna to Sanna.

00:38:22.000 --> 00:38:24.000
Don't you remember?

00:38:24.000 --> 00:38:26.000
Three stars, two stars.

00:38:31.000 --> 00:38:32.000
Now.

00:38:35.000 --> 00:38:37.000
This is a strange day.

00:38:37.000 --> 00:38:39.000
When does the day begin?

00:38:41.000 --> 00:38:43.000
In the evening.

00:38:43.000 --> 00:38:45.000
And when does it finish?

00:38:46.000 --> 00:38:47.000
No!

00:38:47.000 --> 00:38:48.000
No!

00:38:48.000 --> 00:38:50.000
It doesn't finish at darkness.

00:38:50.000 --> 00:38:51.000
Read it carefully.

00:38:51.000 --> 00:38:53.000
This end, we're reading Hebrew.

00:38:54.000 --> 00:38:57.000
And in Hebrew, the reader is attentive.

00:38:58.000 --> 00:39:00.000
It finishes in the morning.

00:39:01.000 --> 00:39:03.000
It finishes in the morning.

00:39:03.000 --> 00:39:05.000
Vaya erev, vay mokher.

00:39:06.000 --> 00:39:08.000
There was evening and there was morning.

00:39:08.000 --> 00:39:11.000
I said there was evening and there was evening.

00:39:11.000 --> 00:39:13.000
There was evening and there was morning.

00:39:15.000 --> 00:39:17.000
What does it say?

00:39:18.000 --> 00:39:23.000
There was evening and there was morning.

00:39:27.000 --> 00:39:29.000
Yeah, it's written there.

00:39:29.000 --> 00:39:31.000
It's written there.

00:39:32.000 --> 00:39:35.000
Do you remember this very famous American writer?

00:39:35.000 --> 00:39:37.000
I think he was the first one.

00:39:37.000 --> 00:39:40.000
Edgar Avril Holt.

00:39:40.000 --> 00:39:42.000
He wrote a police story.

00:39:42.000 --> 00:39:44.000
Do you remember?

00:39:45.000 --> 00:39:46.000
He wrote many kinds of stories.

00:39:46.000 --> 00:39:47.000
He was a great writer.

00:39:47.000 --> 00:39:49.000
But he wrote police mystery stories.

00:39:50.000 --> 00:39:55.000
And he was the first one who wrote mystery stories.

00:39:56.000 --> 00:40:00.000
Now, when you write, when you produce a new type of literature,

00:40:01.000 --> 00:40:04.000
what is important, otherwise you don't produce the literature,

00:40:04.000 --> 00:40:07.000
is to produce a new kind of reader.

00:40:08.000 --> 00:40:10.000
Without the reader of police stories,

00:40:10.000 --> 00:40:12.000
there would be no police stories.

00:40:12.000 --> 00:40:14.000
When you read a police story,

00:40:14.000 --> 00:40:16.000
you read it differently than when you read, I don't know,

00:40:16.000 --> 00:40:18.000
the New York Times.

00:40:18.000 --> 00:40:19.000
Right?

00:40:21.000 --> 00:40:24.000
The Hebrew scripture is not just a book,

00:40:24.000 --> 00:40:27.000
because it created a new kind of a reader.

00:40:28.000 --> 00:40:31.000
Without this kind of reader, the book does not exist.

00:40:31.000 --> 00:40:35.000
So, if you wanted to read the Bible,

00:40:35.000 --> 00:40:37.000
well, you have to read it in a special way,

00:40:37.000 --> 00:40:39.000
in which every word, everything,

00:40:40.000 --> 00:40:42.000
you have to be in the tone.

00:40:43.000 --> 00:40:44.000
Right?

00:40:44.000 --> 00:40:46.000
So, again, somebody wanted to answer,

00:40:46.000 --> 00:40:49.000
what is the special, what kind of a world of a day is this?

00:40:50.000 --> 00:40:52.000
It ends in morning.

00:40:55.000 --> 00:40:56.000
Is it?

00:41:01.000 --> 00:41:02.000
It's not 25.

00:41:03.000 --> 00:41:04.000
That's true.

00:41:04.000 --> 00:41:06.000
I don't know why it's not 25.

00:41:07.000 --> 00:41:08.000
Because there was no sun.

00:41:08.000 --> 00:41:10.000
You see, the sun comes later.

00:41:11.000 --> 00:41:13.000
But this is a different kind of a day.

00:41:13.000 --> 00:41:14.000
How do you know?

00:41:15.000 --> 00:41:17.000
It begins with evening.

00:41:18.000 --> 00:41:21.000
And it grows and grows and grows

00:41:21.000 --> 00:41:23.000
until it becomes morning.

00:41:25.000 --> 00:41:28.000
It is a development of something.

00:41:30.000 --> 00:41:32.000
It is a structure of something.

00:41:33.000 --> 00:41:36.000
And this morning, the morning of the first day,

00:41:36.000 --> 00:41:38.000
will be the evening of the second day.

00:41:40.000 --> 00:41:42.000
The second day is a different state.

00:41:43.000 --> 00:41:45.000
And the morning of the second day

00:41:46.000 --> 00:41:48.000
is the evening of the third day.

00:41:50.000 --> 00:41:52.000
So, here you see it in a very careful way,

00:41:52.000 --> 00:41:55.000
without discussing science, religion,

00:41:55.000 --> 00:42:00.000
you have to read the Hebrew scripture carefully.

00:42:01.000 --> 00:42:03.000
And it tells you a lot.

00:42:03.000 --> 00:42:06.000
It tells you we're not talking about a 24-hour day.

00:42:08.000 --> 00:42:10.000
We're taking the word day here

00:42:10.000 --> 00:42:12.000
in a very metaphoric way.

00:42:13.000 --> 00:42:15.000
And we're talking about a day

00:42:15.000 --> 00:42:17.000
that begins in darkness

00:42:18.000 --> 00:42:20.000
and ends in the morning,

00:42:20.000 --> 00:42:21.000
after sunrise.

00:42:22.000 --> 00:42:24.000
Like a new epoch.

00:42:24.000 --> 00:42:25.000
It's an epoch.

00:42:25.000 --> 00:42:26.000
It's a state.

00:42:28.000 --> 00:42:30.000
And it finishes in the zenith,

00:42:30.000 --> 00:42:32.000
in the culmination of

00:42:33.000 --> 00:42:34.000
the morning.

00:42:37.000 --> 00:42:38.000
You understand?

00:42:38.000 --> 00:42:40.000
Very, very

00:42:43.000 --> 00:42:44.000
careful.

00:42:44.000 --> 00:42:46.000
Very exact.

00:42:46.000 --> 00:42:47.000
Very precise.

00:42:49.000 --> 00:42:51.000
Well, what's your experience

00:42:51.000 --> 00:42:53.000
after one day of creation?

00:42:54.000 --> 00:42:56.000
Is this what you expected?

00:42:57.000 --> 00:42:59.000
Shall we continue to the second day of creation

00:42:59.000 --> 00:43:01.000
or should we read something else?

00:43:01.000 --> 00:43:03.000
We'll find out how it ends.

00:43:03.000 --> 00:43:04.000
How it ends?

00:43:04.000 --> 00:43:05.000
I hope not.

00:43:08.000 --> 00:43:09.000
Is it so fine?

00:43:09.000 --> 00:43:10.000
Is this what you want to do?

00:43:10.000 --> 00:43:11.000
All right.

00:43:13.000 --> 00:43:15.000
Well, we're going to go

00:43:15.000 --> 00:43:16.000
into

00:43:17.000 --> 00:43:18.000
the second day.

00:43:20.000 --> 00:43:22.000
We had said something about

00:43:22.000 --> 00:43:23.000
the Earth.

00:43:24.000 --> 00:43:26.000
The focus of our attention

00:43:26.000 --> 00:43:27.000
is not heavens.

00:43:28.000 --> 00:43:30.000
Only what we need to know

00:43:30.000 --> 00:43:31.000
is

00:43:35.000 --> 00:43:37.000
that the Earth is part of something else.

00:43:37.000 --> 00:43:38.000
Something we call,

00:43:38.000 --> 00:43:40.000
our universe is called Samai.

00:43:41.000 --> 00:43:42.000
And

00:43:43.000 --> 00:43:45.000
now we're focusing on the Earth.

00:43:45.000 --> 00:43:47.000
You see somehow there is

00:43:47.000 --> 00:43:49.000
a sort of order

00:43:49.000 --> 00:43:51.000
that we don't have before

00:43:51.000 --> 00:43:53.000
in a state of total chaos.

00:43:54.000 --> 00:43:56.000
Bayom el-enohim.

00:43:57.000 --> 00:43:59.000
Elohim, again, speak.

00:43:59.000 --> 00:44:01.000
Never had to do with

00:44:01.000 --> 00:44:03.000
order, physics, nature.

00:44:05.000 --> 00:44:07.000
Yehi rakia

00:44:07.000 --> 00:44:09.000
betok samai.

00:44:10.000 --> 00:44:12.000
Somehow, all of a sudden we discover

00:44:13.000 --> 00:44:15.000
that this planet Earth

00:44:16.000 --> 00:44:18.000
was all covered by water.

00:44:20.000 --> 00:44:22.000
Totally covered by water.

00:44:24.000 --> 00:44:26.000
And God wants to make a rakia

00:44:27.000 --> 00:44:29.000
to create the space between the water.

00:44:31.000 --> 00:44:33.000
And separate some water into

00:44:33.000 --> 00:44:35.000
a boat.

00:44:36.000 --> 00:44:37.000
Put it out.

00:44:38.000 --> 00:44:40.000
And some water is going to remain here on Earth.

00:44:40.000 --> 00:44:42.000
And somehow there is a pressure

00:44:42.000 --> 00:44:44.000
between what there is

00:44:44.000 --> 00:44:47.000
below and what God pushes above.

00:44:48.000 --> 00:44:50.000
And that is going to be called the atmosphere.

00:44:53.000 --> 00:44:55.000
All that makes a space.

00:44:56.000 --> 00:44:58.000
Somehow there was a force of pulling

00:44:58.000 --> 00:45:00.000
and it breaks the space.

00:45:01.000 --> 00:45:03.000
And now there is

00:45:03.000 --> 00:45:05.000
a space.

00:45:05.000 --> 00:45:07.000
That creates space.

00:45:07.000 --> 00:45:09.000
Interesting.

00:45:09.000 --> 00:45:11.000
Here for the universe you see that the space

00:45:11.000 --> 00:45:13.000
is not something...

00:45:13.000 --> 00:45:15.000
It's not the absence of something.

00:45:15.000 --> 00:45:17.000
It's not something dead.

00:45:17.000 --> 00:45:19.000
It's not something geometric.

00:45:19.000 --> 00:45:21.000
But it's like two forces pulling

00:45:21.000 --> 00:45:23.000
in different directions.

00:45:23.000 --> 00:45:25.000
Creating a space.

00:45:27.000 --> 00:45:29.000
And rakia literally means...

00:45:29.000 --> 00:45:31.000
It doesn't mean space like in English.

00:45:32.000 --> 00:45:34.000
The rakia in Hebrew means to stretch.

00:45:34.000 --> 00:45:36.000
It stretches.

00:45:36.000 --> 00:45:38.000
Like you are making pulling.

00:45:40.000 --> 00:45:42.000
And it creates...

00:45:42.000 --> 00:45:44.000
By doing this pulling

00:45:44.000 --> 00:45:46.000
it creates a hyperspace.

00:45:46.000 --> 00:45:48.000
There is a pull from above

00:45:48.000 --> 00:45:50.000
and a pull from below.

00:45:50.000 --> 00:45:52.000
Between these two pulls

00:45:52.000 --> 00:45:54.000
there is a hyperspace.

00:45:54.000 --> 00:45:56.000
But the word in Hebrew for space, rakia,

00:45:56.000 --> 00:45:58.000
is to stretch, to pull.

00:45:59.000 --> 00:46:01.000
Very interesting.

00:46:03.000 --> 00:46:05.000
Now, it says,

00:46:05.000 --> 00:46:07.000
let it be rakia.

00:46:07.000 --> 00:46:09.000
They talk of mind.

00:46:09.000 --> 00:46:11.000
By himadil, the mind, the mind.

00:46:12.000 --> 00:46:14.000
And therefore let it be a separation.

